{
  "description": "Thirty-second calibration and validation cases for a topology-aware predictive RealSense resource model.",
  "notes": [
    "All cases use 30 warm-up frames and a fixed 30-second measurement window.",
    "D455 x2 uses two cameras behind one powered hub and one root xHCI controller.",
    "D455 x3 concentrated and split-controller cases are held-out validation points; their userspace demand is predicted from the D455 x1 and x2 calibration cells before measurement, while USB payload and xHCI IRQ demand are reported per controller.",
    "Mixed x4 uses three D455 cameras and one D435, with two cameras behind each powered hub/root xHCI controller.",
    "The common 60 FPS profile enables depth, IR1, and IR2 but disables color so D435 and D455 measurements use the same stream profile; preflight established that this profile is an overload point for two D455 cameras on one controller and for the balanced four-camera topology.",
    "The four-camera ladder adds depth-only 60 FPS, depth plus IR at 30 FPS, and depth plus color at 60 FPS to separate USB payload, activation-rate, and stream-composition effects.",
    "The all-stream 60 FPS four-camera point is retained as an explicit overload case after three fresh-start attempts failed its warm-up freshness gate."
  ],
